{"slug":"floyd-spence","qid":"Q1430393","name":"Floyd Spence","desc":"American politician (1928–2001)","article":"Floyd Spence","born":"1928-04-09","died":"2001-08-16","birthplace":"Columbia","parties":["Republican Party","Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"SC-02","f":1971,"u":2001},{"t":"South Carolina Senate","w":"","f":1967,"u":1970},{"t":"South Carolina House of Representatives","w":"","f":1956,"u":1962}],"summary":"Floyd Davidson Spence (April 9, 1928 – August 16, 2001) was an American attorney and a politician from the U.S. state of South Carolina. Elected for three terms to the South Carolina House of Representatives from Lexington County as a Democrat, in 1962 Spence announced his decision to switch to the Republican Party, as he was unhappy with shifts in the national party.\nHe lost a contested seat that year for United States Representative from South Carolina's 2nd congressional district to Democrat Albert W. Watson, who had the support of powerful senator Strom Thurmond.","photo":null,"history":[{"y":2000,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":154338,"s":56.96,"w":true,"n":"Floyd Spence"},{"y":1998,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":119538,"s":57.83,"w":true,"n":"Floyd Spence"},{"y":1996,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":158229,"s":89.93,"w":true,"n":"Floyd Spence"},{"y":1994,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":133307,"s":99.79,"w":true,"n":"Floyd Spence"},{"y":1992,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":148667,"s":87.62,"w":true,"n":"Floyd Spence"},{"y":1990,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":90054,"s":88.7,"w":true,"n":"Floyd Spence"},{"y":1988,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":94960,"s":52.76,"w":true,"n":"Floyd D Spence"},{"y":1986,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":73455,"s":53.6,"w":true,"n":"Floyd D Spence"},{"y":1984,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":108085,"s":62.11,"w":true,"n":"Floyd D Spence"},{"y":1982,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":71569,"s":58.51,"w":true,"n":"Floyd D Spence"},{"y":1980,"o":"H","k":"SC-02","p":"R","v":92306,"s":55.72,"w":true,